  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cgi Federal obligated $103M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date, across 32 awards with an average award size of $3.2M. Obligations fell 92.9% year over year compared with the prior full fiscal year. Fiscal history shows obligations of $1.1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1.5B in FY26. The General Services Administration, the Department of Health and Human Services, and the Department of Justice are the top buyers so far, receiving $33.8M, $31.9M, and $21.7M respectively. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest NAICS market for Cgi Federal this year at $65.4M, followed by Facilities Support Services at $15M and Other Computer Related Services at $14.8M. Smaller markets include Computing Infrastructure Providers at $6.2M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $323K. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the figures above are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in award tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Cgi Federal’s obligation level changed this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Cgi Federal obligated $103M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 92.9% year over year compared with the prior period. Fiscal-year history shows a peak of $1.5B in FY26 and then the current $103M partial-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets are driving Cgi Federal’s FY2027 work?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration, the Department of Health and Human Services, and the Department of Justice account for the largest shares of FY2027 obligations at $33.8M, $31.9M, and $21.7M respectively. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $65.4M, with Facilities Support Services at $15M and Other Computer Related Services at $14.8M supporting the total."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Cgi Federal make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Cgi Federal made $103M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Fiscal history shows prior-year obligations of $1.1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1.5B in FY26. The company received 32 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $3.2M."
